# spec: gate-sdk/SPEC.md §Layout and configuration — this repo's gate-sdk knob file; set only what this repo overrides beyond the kit defaults

# spec: gate-sdk/SPEC.md §check-graph — publish the coupling-graph artifact on the docs site (a same-tree served file), not in the workflow dir
GATE_SDK_GRAPH_ARTIFACT = docs/check-graph.html

# spec: gate-sdk/SPEC.md §check-graph — this repo's graph-theme chrome links the docs host and the source repo; sanction those prefixes for the external-ref assertion
GATE_SDK_GRAPH_EXTERNAL_REFS = https://checkwright.dev https://github.com/checkwright

# spec: gate-sdk/SPEC.md §Layout and configuration — where this project publishes the SPEC sections its shipped gate pointers name. The value is the publisher's own and never a kit literal, which is why it lives here beside the host the external-ref sanction already carries: the packer stamps it into the payload and init writes it into a vendored tree's own knob seam, so a consumer whose kit SPECs the payload withholds still reaches the invariant a red gate names
GATE_SDK_SPEC_BASE_URL = https://checkwright.dev

# spec: gate-sdk/SPEC.md §check-shellcheck — this repo ships bash under no kit root: the installer's two bootstraps, its consumer smoke, and the runnable adoption walkthrough; name them so the lint that governs every other script in the tree governs these too. Each directory is named on its own because the gate globs *.sh per named directory and does not descend
GATE_SDK_LINT_EXTRA_DIRS = installer/bin installer/consumer-smoke demo

# spec: gate-sdk/SPEC.md §check-portability-floor — this repo's install-path corpus: the files an adopter's machine actually executes. After the behind-invoke relocation that is `installer/bin` — the two bootstraps, and the whole of the install path written in a shell — plus `gate-sdk/lib/gate.sh`, the one shell `init` leaves behind that the install path runs. Everything else an install performs is Rust and reaches no shell dialect at all. A corpus drawn by directory rather than by reachability is what let a GNU-only primary sit unseen. The vocabulary rides the knob's own default, scripts/portability-patterns.list
GATE_SDK_PORTABILITY_PATHS = installer/bin gate-sdk/lib/gate.sh
